-- title:
--   Coprime Kummer radicand forces n ∣ e(P∣𝔪)
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a discrete valuation ring (a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring), let $R$ be a Dedekind domain which is an $O$-algebra, and let $E$ be a field which is the fraction field of $R$ and an $O$-algebra compatibly, so that $O \to R \to E$ is a tower of algebra maps. Let $\varpi \in O$ be irreducible, $u \in O^{\times}$ a unit, $m \in \mathbb Z$, and $n$ a natural number with $0 < n$ such that $m$ and $n$ are coprime as integers (in the sense of `IsCoprime` over $\mathbb Z$, i.e. the ideal generated by $m$ and $n$ is all of $\mathbb Z$). Suppose there is $a \in E$ with $a^{n} = u \cdot \varpi^{m}$, the right-hand side being formed from the images of $u$ and $\varpi$ under $O \to E$ and an integer power of the latter. Let $\mathfrak P$ be a non-zero prime ideal of $R$ lying over the maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$ of $O$. Then $n$ divides the ramification index of $\mathfrak P$ over $\mathfrak m$ along $O \to R$, in the form `ramificationIdx'`.
--
--   This is the standard ramification computation for a Kummer radicand whose $\varpi$-adic valuation is prime to the exponent: such an element forces every prime above $\mathfrak m$ to have ramification index divisible by $n$, which combined with the fundamental equality yields total ramification. It is used in [`ValuationSubring.forall_comap_eq_imp_eq_and_exists_forall_sub_mem_nonunits_of_pow_eq_of_isCoprime`](thm.html#ValuationSubring.forall_comap_eq_imp_eq_and_exists_forall_sub_mem_nonunits_of_pow_eq_of_isCoprime).
